  "principles": [
    "Linguistic markers have priority over semantic/content shifts.",
    "Participant change is scene-transition evidence but not automatic macro hierarchy.",
    "Hierarchy level depends on surrounding opening/ending/enclosure evidence.",
    "The same linguistic formula may support the same structural function.",
    "The same marker family does not automatically imply the same hierarchy level.",
    "Absence of an explicit marker can prevent a semantic shift from becoming a structural boundary.",
    "Parallel endings may be human-recognized formal evidence without being promoted into MR1 explicit closure rules.",
    "Computational evidence and human structural adjudication remain separate.",
    "Boundary and discourse continuity are distinct.",
    "Not macro-level does not mean subordinate."
